{
  "configuration_id": "config_039",
  "reason": "The current best is config_033 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, weighted) at 0.7131 accuracy. The image modality contributes meaningfully in the multimodal setting (~0.06 gain over RNA-only transformer multiprofile at 0.6530), yet the image-only ResNet50 baseline was very weak (0.2079), suggesting the image encoder quality may be a bottleneck. Config_039 makes a single clean change—swapping ResNet50 for the stronger ViT-L image encoder—while keeping all other settings at their best-known values (scvi_n200, multiprofile, transformer aggregation, weighted fusion). This isolates the effect of image encoder quality on multimodal fusion performance. It is the best use of this experiment because it exploits the strongest identified direction (weighted multimodal fusion) with a logical, single-variable extension that has the highest expected upside, and if it succeeds, the remaining 2 experiments can further refine around the new best."
}

